{"step_index":24,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-20T17:43:06Z","content":"The full forensic analysis is in [forensic-analysis.md](file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/66d91e76-c909-4add-a716-4a4f76804b83/forensic-analysis.md).\n\n**All three are upgrades.** Here's the short version:\n\n### Anti-Sycophancy: UPGRADE\n- Adds a **challenge-response canary** (the `check N` system) that the original couldn't do\n- Adds **blind second opinion** for high-stakes decisions — the strongest anti-drift technique possible\n- Adds the **flip test** (\"if he argued the opposite, would your verdict change?\")\n- Correctly separates judgement from prose style (banned vocabulary list → delegated to stop-slop/humanizer where it belongs)\n- Frames calibration as \"be accurate, not contrarian\" — prevents the original's failure mode of performative disagreement\n\n### Deep Researcher: UPGRADE\n- Fixes the original's core weakness: it was good at *collecting* but weak at *verifying*\n- Adds **tool call budgets** (prevents runaway research sessions)\n- Adds **lateral reading** (\"judge a source by leaving it\") — how professional fact-checkers actually work\n- Replaces rigid tier classification with reasoning about *independence and first-hand access*\n- Adds a **worked example** showing how a real statistic mutates across the internet\n- Adds **evidence-by-question-type.md** — domain-specific source hierarchies the original never had\n\n### Prompt Forge: UPGRADE\n- **Two-output architecture** (faithful rewrite + gap report, hard-separated) prevents the #1 failure: silently changing the user's intent\n- **Coverage check** with exact item count — verifiable, not vibes\n- **\"What the model will guess\"** section — shows the user the default answer they're about to get\n- Removes template auto-selection (correct — current models don't need CO-STAR/RISEN scaffolding)\n- Evidence-based \"what stays out\" list (expert roles don't help accuracy, \"think step by step\" is redundant on reasoning models)\n\nThe pattern: shorter files, but **principles over checklists**, grounded in real failure modes, cleanly scoped across skills, and built for frontier models that generalise from understanding better than they follow long rule lists."}
